    "question": {
      ":question/id": "f9a3a402-a27a-5cd6-b485-3c6f136953f5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $4\\times 4$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim(Null(}A))=1,$ then $\\text{rank}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=4.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ \\text{rank}(A)+1 & =4 \\\\ \\text{rank}(A) & =4-1 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "83ffeacf-3f0d-5465-b1c5-ea210e601329",
